Subject: [PATCH] Explain and repair group creation failures, tidy code, add
 project docs

Creating a group failed with a generic "Something went wrong" whenever the
connected database was missing migrations, or the signed-in account had no
profile row. Both are now reported clearly, and a new migration creates
missing profiles and re-asserts the sign-up trigger.

- server/errors.js: schema mismatches return 503 with a pointer to the
  troubleshooting guide; a missing profile returns a specific message
- supabase: add 20261124000000_backfill_profiles.sql
- client: reformat the poll screens and data layer for readability, with
  clearer errors for a missing poll or an out-of-date database
- tests: fix a stale option count in the RLS suite, add a regression test
  for the missing-profile case, run each suite from its own script
- CI: run the RLS and voting tests against local Supabase
- docs: rewrite the README and add architecture, Supabase, database and
  development guides; rename the proposal PDF

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
